const e="kerala-school-sasthrolsavam-work-experience-fair",h=2025,t="Read in full from the Kerala School Sasthrolsavam Manual 2025 (Malayalam; 250 PDF pages): Chapters 1-5 (common rules, levels, committees, appeals, championship), Chapter 9 (Work Experience Fair) with Annexure 1 (LP and UP items) and Annexure 2 (HS, HSS and VHSS items), and the entry forms. The manual is in a legacy font, so every page was read from its image; page numbers in Source are the printed numbers. The manual prints no dates for the festival, no venue or address, no phone numbers or e-mail, no website for the online entry, no last date to register, and no cash amount for the prizes. These are not captured. The only dated item is the order of 12 September 2025 (a news Variable). Amounts printed (appeal fees, the registration fee of the sub-district fair, the fee for a new certificate, the affiliation fees of the associations) are Variables. The single evaluation table printed for every on-the-spot item (workload 40, skill 25, knowledge 20, social use 15) is kept once under Judges and Judging, not repeated per item. The manual says the exhibition competition is held between 'classes' and the construction competition between students; this is kept as printed. Where the LP and UP items and the HS items repeat the same instruction, it is written once in the competition row; level differences (card board numbers, fabric printing sizes, book binding, thread pattern boards, puppets) are in the competition and age group rows. The manual also holds the Special School Work Experience items and the Kerala School Skill Festival; they are named in one line each under Other Parts of the Manual. The manual's Annexure 2 list is 35 items and the template has the same 35 items; Annexure 1 is 25 items and the template carries all 25.",n=JSON.parse('{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Kerala School Sasthrolsavam, Work Experience Fair. Read these rules before you register.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"The Work Experience Fair is held for LP, UP, HS and HSS/VHSS children at the school, sub-district, revenue district and state levels. Every item is an on-the-spot construction competition of 3 hours. The head master or principal makes the online entries.","Notes":["A child can take part in only one item of one fair, and in the quiz of one field.","Bring all the unprocessed materials and the tools for your item. Do not bring made parts unless the item says you may.","The competition starts at {{OnTheSpotStartTime}}. Competitors must also take part in the exhibition.","Upload the photo of every child when the entry is made.","A complaint about a result must be given within one hour after the result is announced."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["The Kerala School Sasthrolsavam is the Science, Mathematics, Social Science, Work Experience and IT fair of the children in LP, UP, HS, Higher Secondary and Vocational Higher Secondary classes of the Government, Aided and Unaided (recognised) schools of Kerala under the General Education Department.","All earlier Science, Maths, Social Science, Work Experience and IT fair manuals and amendments are cancelled by this manual.","The competitions are held from school level to state level on the dates in the education calendar that the department publishes each year, or on the dates the Director of General Education gives.","The fair of each school is held by the clubs of the school. The fairs of the sub-district and revenue district are held by the club associations or councils of that level. The state fair is held by the department and the state club associations or councils.","The Director of General Education gives the directions needed to run the Kerala School Sasthrolsavam.","The fairs are held on the subject that is told from time to time under the rules and directions of the General Education Department.","Aim: to grow scientific, mathematical, social science, work experience and IT interest and research interest in the children, and to grow what they learn in a way that helps the society they live in.","Aim: to train the children to use well in daily life the knowledge they gain from science and technology, mathematics, social science, work experience and IT.","Aim: to help the children know the link between people and their surroundings and understand the method of gaining this knowledge.","Aim: to grow the inquiry mind and the research mind along with the gain of knowledge.","Aim: to find and nurture the natural abilities of the children.","Aim: to understand current events against the background of past and lasting history, and to keep them for the future generation in a useful way.","Aim: to introduce the importance and use of free software.","Aim: to give chances to know new technical fields in IT and use them, to do creative work with digital media, and to practise a computer language.","Aim: to make the children able to win their own scientific and technical achievements in the future, and to gain practical skill in science, maths, social science, work experience and IT.","The Work Experience Fair has two parts: the on-the-spot construction competition and the exhibition competition.","In the on-the-spot construction competition, each item takes at most 3 hours. A competitor can take part in only one item.","Only the items given in the annexures of the manual can be held. No item that is not in the annexure can be put in the competition.","Annexure 1 gives the on-the-spot items for LP and UP. Annexure 2 gives the on-the-spot items for HS, HSS and VHSS.","All the unprocessed materials and the tools for the on-the-spot competition must be brought by the competitors. At the state level too, the competitors bring them.","In an on-the-spot competition, the marking, cutting, shaping and joining that an item needs are done at the competition place, as each item says. Parts or products made earlier are not accepted unless an item says so.","Where an item says that electric tools or electrical machines are not allowed, only hand tools are used.","The Work Experience Fair of Special School students is held along with the Kerala School Work Experience Fair. Special schools have separate competitions at the state level, so their children cannot take part in the general school fair.","The state fair is planned in three days. On the first day the competition of the Special School children is held, on the second day the HS section and on the third day the HSS and VHSS section."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["Children of the Government, Aided and Unaided (recognised) schools under the General Education Department of Kerala can take part.","The competition is held in four categories by class. Category I is class 1 to 4 (LP). Category II is class 5 to 7 (UP). Category III is class 8 to 10 (HS). Category IV is class 11 and 12 (HSS and VHSS).","Category I and II competitions end at the sub-district level. Category III and IV competitions go up to the state level.","A school fair is open to every child of the school. Every child gets the chance to take part by category.","Only a competitor who got first place with an A grade in the item at the school fair can take part in the sub-district competition.","In Category III and IV, only a competitor who got the first or second place with an A grade at the sub-district level can take part in the revenue district competition, and only a competitor who got the first or second place with an A grade at the revenue district level can take part in the state competition.","A child can take part in only one item of one of the five fairs (Science, Maths, Social Science, Work Experience, IT). In addition, the child can take part in the quiz competition of any one field.","A competitor with marks below 60 percent in an item gets no grade. If only one child takes part in an item, the child goes to the sub-district fair only if the performance is good enough for a grade.","If nobody gets first place with an A grade in an item at the school fair, no competitor is sent from the school to the sub-district fair for that item.","If two competitors get equal marks for the first or the second place in an item at the school fair, the competitor for the upper level is chosen by the total marks of the evaluation plus the marks for evaluation criterion (A).","A school can take part at the sub-district level only if it is affiliated to the science, maths, social science, work experience and IT club association or council of that sub-district.","A sub-district can take part at the revenue district level only if it is affiliated to the club association or council of that revenue district.","All district level clubs of a revenue district must be affiliated to the state club association or council before the revenue district takes part in the state fair.","At the sub-district fair, the competitor brings the school level certificate that the head master or principal of the school has attested.","At the revenue district fair, the competitor brings the certificate of recognition from the head master or principal of the school, attested by the sub-district education officer.","At the state fair, the competitor brings the certificate of recognition from the head master or principal of the school, attested by the Deputy Director of Education.","Only two competitors from a sub-district or a revenue district can take part in an item at the next higher level, on merit.","Before a court or an appeal authority gives an order on a request of a competitor, it must be made sure that only two competitors take part at the higher level and that the third competitor does not come. If a court or an appeal authority allows a third competitor by a clear order, the performance of the competitors who already qualified is evaluated again, one is left out, and only two from one place take part in an item at the higher level (High Court judgment W.A. No. 1178/2017 dated 22.6.2017).","Each school at the sub-district fair brings an escorting teacher. If girls take part, a woman teacher must go with the team as an escorting teacher. The teachers carry the full responsibility for the children.","The Work Experience Fair has the LP section (classes 1 to 4), the UP section (classes 5 to 7), the HS section (classes 8 to 10) and the HSS and VHSS section (classes 11 and 12).","At the school level, LP and UP follow the items of Annexure 1. HS, HSS and VHSS follow the items of Annexure 2. A child can take part in only one item of the on-the-spot construction competition.","The competitors of the on-the-spot competition must also take part in the exhibition competition.","At the sub-district level, a school can take part in at most 10 items in LP and at most 10 items in UP. At the sub-district level, a school can take part in at most 20 items in HS, and at most 20 items in HSS and VHSS.","Only a competitor who got first place in an item of Annexure 1 at the school fair can take part in the sub-district on-the-spot construction competition.","Only HS, HSS and VHSS competitors who got first or second place with an A grade in an item at the sub-district fair can take part in the revenue district on-the-spot competition.","Only HS, HSS and VHSS competitors who got first or second place with an A grade in an item at the revenue district fair can take part in the state on-the-spot competition."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["All competitions from the sub-district level to the state level, including the club level competitions, are held on the online system. The head master or principal makes the online entry of the children with great care.","The photo of every child must be uploaded at the time of registration.","The full responsibility for the online entries is with the head master or principal.","After the sub-district competitions, the list of the competitors chosen for the revenue district competitions is registered online.","The state fair registration committee registers the teams that come from the different districts, gives the registration cards and passes their details to the accommodation committee. It also gives the food coupons to the committees and the team managers.","At the state fair, each competitor gives a short description of the exhibit, with photos, at the time of the competition.","Competitors must come to the place of the competition on the time fixed. A competitor who does not come on time can be made ineligible.","The rules and conditions of each competition item are announced on the stage before the competition starts.","The programme committee gives the code numbers for the competitors from the office of the Director of General Education.","The entry forms of the manual give the details of the school, the competitors and the escorting teachers. The sub-district entry form carries the school name and school (Sampoorna) code, the type of school (Government, Aided or Unaided), the number of boys, girls and others, and the name, designation, phone number and signature of the escorting teacher, with the signature of the head of the institution. The head of the school also signs a declaration that the details agree with the school records and with the manual.","The revenue district and state entry forms carry the name of the sub-district or revenue district, the number of boys and girls, the name of each item, the name of each child in capital letters, the name of the school, the class, the sex and remarks. The state fair form also names the team manager and the escorting teachers with their addresses and carries the signature and seal of the Deputy Director of Education.","The sub-district entry form for LP and UP (Form IV B) names the sub-district, the venue and the dates of the fair, the school and its school (Sampoorna) code, and the items (25 on-the-spot items), with the name of the student, the name of the school, the class, the sex and remarks for two entries in each item.","The revenue district entry form for HS and HSS/VHSS (Form IV B-2) names the revenue district, the venue and the dates, and the items (35 on-the-spot items), with the name of the student, the name of the school, the class, the sex and remarks for two entries in each item.","Each entry form also gives the name and address of the team manager and the name and address of three escorting teachers, with the place, date, signature, the seal and the signature of the Deputy Director of Education of the district.","The evaluation sheet of the exhibition competition names the item, the code number of the students, and the marks for arrangement of the exhibits (5), knowledge of marketing potential and price (3) and knowledge of the social usefulness of the product (2), out of 10 in all."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees and Payment","Items":["A registration fee of {{SubDistrictRegistrationFee}} can be collected at the sub-district fair.","The funds for the sub-district fair come from the scheme fund, the special fee fund, public donations, the funds of the science, maths, social science, work experience and IT clubs, and PTA donations.","The funds are spent as per the budget that the organising committee approves. The accounts of the fair are presented to the concerned committee and passed within one month after the fair.","The income and expenses of the funds that the scheme gives are approved by the organising committee within one month after the fair, and then given to the treasury of the education officer.","At state level, the Finance Committee gives the budget of all committees to the organising committee for approval, allows unexpected expenses in advance (to be approved later), and helps the General Convener to prepare the accounts for audit. The audited accounts are approved by the organising committee within one month after the fair.","The committees can take gifts and donations of articles as the organising committee approves. A special register is kept for this and the General Convener signs it.","An appeal costs a fee that depends on the level. There is no appeal fee at the school level (see Complaints and Appeals).","The fee for a new certificate is given under Prizes and Certificates.","Sub-district Work Experience Association or Council: each school pays an affiliation fee (a separate amount for each club). A UP school pays {{AffiliationFeeUP}}, a high school pays {{AffiliationFeeHS}} and an HSS or VHSS school pays {{AffiliationFeeHSS}}.","The sub-district association pays 25 percent of the affiliation fees it receives to the revenue district association.","Each revenue district must be affiliated to the state Work Experience Association or Council by paying {{StateAffiliationFee}}.","The secretary of each association keeps the funds and the accounts, presents the budget in the general body, and prepares the yearly income and expense account, the report and the yearly plan for the approval of the general body."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Time Schedule","Items":["The on-the-spot construction competition starts at {{OnTheSpotStartTime}} and ends at {{OnTheSpotEndTime}}.","The final evaluation of the on-the-spot competition is done until {{FinalEvaluationEndTime}}.","From {{FinalEvaluationEndTime}} to {{LunchEndTime}} the competitors have lunch and prepare for the exhibition competition.","The exhibition competition and its evaluation run until {{ExhibitionEndTime}}.","The public can see the products from {{PublicViewingStartTime}} to {{ExhibitionEndTime}}.","The dates and the venue of each fair are decided at each level by the committee in charge, as the levels section says. The manual prints none for 2025."]},{"Key":"levels","Title":"Levels and Qualification","Items":["The Sasthrolsavam has four levels: school, sub-district, revenue district and state.","School level: the fair is held in one day under the science, maths, social science, work experience and IT clubs of the school. Every child of the school gets the chance to take part by category.","The school fair committee has the ward member as chairman, the PTA president or the SMC chairman as vice chairman, the principal or the first teacher as General Convener, the first teacher or the senior assistant as joint General Convener, the club coordinators as joint convenors, and all teachers, PTA and SMC members, mother PTA members and the school leader as members. Sub-committees can be formed.","Sub-district level (LP, UP, HS, HSS and VHSS): the fair is held in two days. The sub-district education officer, the RDD or AD of Higher Secondary and Vocational Higher Secondary, and the club secretaries choose a suitable school together. The sub-district clubs hold the fair. There are separate competitions for LP, UP, HS and HSS/VHSS, and HSS and VHSS are one unit.","Sub-district winners get certificates and encouragement awards.","The sub-district organising committee has the MPs, MLAs, and the presidents of district, block and grama panchayats, the mayor and the municipal chairmen as patrons; the mayor, municipal chairman or grama panchayat president as chairman; the principal or head master of the venue school as General Convener; the club secretaries as convenors; and the sub-district education officer as treasurer.","Revenue district level (HS, HSS and VHSS): the committees are formed by the Deputy Directors of Education. The fair is held in two days. The Deputy Director of Education, the RDD, the AD and the club secretaries, with the Kite district coordinator, choose suitable schools together. All sub-districts of the revenue district must take part.","At the revenue district fair, HS and HSS/VHSS are evaluated separately. The evaluation records are kept for one year in the office of the Deputy Director of Education. Winners get certificates and encouragement awards.","The revenue district organising committee has the ministers, MPs, MLAs, district panchayat president, mayor, municipal chairmen, District Collector and District Police Chief as patrons; the local MLA as chairman; the Deputy Director of Education as General Convener; and the District Educational Officer of the education district as treasurer.","State level (HS, HSS and VHSS): the fair is held in three days under the General Education Department and the state science, maths, social science, work experience and IT association or council. The Director of General Education decides the place of the fair. All revenue districts of the state must take part.","At the state fair the first three places in each item get certificates, cash awards and honours.","The state organising committee has the Governor, the Chief Minister, the Leader of the Opposition, the Minister of General Education and the ministers of the host district as chief patrons. The Director of General Education is the General Coordinator and the Additional Director of General Education (Academic) is the General Convener.","The state organising (co-ordination) committee is fully responsible for the state fair. It prepares the budget, approves the sums for the sub-committees, approves the income and expense plan of the finance committee, and joins all sub-committees to work together.","The state sub-committees are the Programme, Reception, Exhibition and Cultural, Food, Pandal and Stage, Finance, Publicity, Law and Order, Welfare, Registration, Accommodation, Transport, Trophy, Light and Sound, Souvenir and Green Protocol committees.","School level: the on-the-spot construction competition and the exhibition competition are held. LP and UP follow Annexure 1. HS, HSS and VHSS follow Annexure 2.","LP and UP: the competition ends at the sub-district level. At the sub-district level there is no exhibition competition. The competitors take part in the on-the-spot construction competition only.","HS, HSS and VHSS: the competition goes up to the state level. At the revenue district fair and at the state fair there is an exhibition competition too.","At the revenue district fair, the products of all the on-the-spot competitions are put in the exhibition, and the exhibition competition is held.","At the state fair, the exhibition competition is held on the revenue district basis. The HS and the HSS/VHSS competitors of one revenue district take part in the exhibition together.","At the state level, the products of the on-the-spot construction competition (Annexure 2) are all put in the exhibition. The exhibits are shown at the place where the on-the-spot competition was held, so that the exhibition competition can be evaluated.","The competitors can leave the competition place only after the exhibition competition has been evaluated.","Work Experience Associations and Councils: the sub-district Association or Council (a general body of the Work Experience teachers, with an executive committee of the sub-district education officer as president, vice presidents from the principals, first teachers, UP and LP head masters, a secretary, a joint secretary and 4 members) runs the sub-district activities and organises the quiz competitions, fairs, seminars, discussion classes, workshops and talent search examination. Its term is 2 years.","The revenue district Work Experience Association or Council (RDWECA) has the Deputy Director of Education as president and the District Education Officers as vice presidents. Its secretary is chosen from the sub-district secretaries. It has 3 joint secretaries and the members are the sub-district secretaries, with two members the Deputy Director nominates. Its term is 2 years.","The state Work Experience Association or Council (KSSCA, KSMCA, KSSSCA, KSWECA) has its office in the Directorate of General Education. Its executive committee has the Director of General Education as president, the Additional Director (Academic) as vice president, the Deputy Director as general secretary, one revenue district secretary as secretary, another as joint secretary and 6 members (3 revenue district secretaries and 2 experts of the general body nominated by the Director). Its term is 2 years.","Each association or council takes its decisions on the directions of the Director of General Education. The state general body has the right to change these rules when needed."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Team Managers and Escorting Teachers","Items":["Each school at the sub-district fair brings an escorting teacher with its team. If girls take part, a woman teacher must go with the team as an escorting teacher.","At the revenue district fair, the team manager of each sub-district team is the sub-district education officer, and the joint team manager is the sub-district secretary of the club association.","At the state fair, each revenue district team has a team manager. Each section has escorting teachers. The secretaries of the district associations are joint team managers. Women teachers go with the girls."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Points and Grading","Items":["A competitor who gets 60 percent marks or more in an item gets a grade. Grade A is 80 percent or more and gives 5 points. Grade B is 70 percent to 79 percent and gives 3 points. Grade C is 60 percent to 69 percent and gives 1 point.","Items that get less than 60 percent marks are not graded.","Place points: the first place gets 5 points, the second place gets 3 points and the third place gets 1 point.","For the overall championship, the total of the grade points and the place points is counted. If the totals are equal, the number of first places is counted.","Sub-district level: the best school in each of LP, UP, HS and HSS/VHSS is found from the total points of all the fairs. The schools with the best show in each of the Science, Maths, Social Science, Work Experience and IT fairs are also found.","Revenue district level: the best sub-districts and the best schools are found. The championship of HS and of HSS/VHSS is decided from the total points of the five fairs. The schools and sub-districts with the best show in each fair are also found.","State level: the best districts, sub-districts and schools are found. The championship of HS and of HSS/VHSS is decided from the total points of the five fairs. The districts and schools with the best show in each fair are also found.","Only the competition items that are part of a fair count for the championship of that fair.","The champion is decided from the marks of the on-the-spot construction competition and the marks of the exhibition competition together.","For the Work Experience Fair, the points of every on-the-spot item and of the exhibition are counted for the championship.","At the school, sub-district and revenue district levels, the exhibition competition is held between classes and the construction competition between individual students (as printed in the manual). Classes that get the first, second and third place in the exhibition, and students that get the first, second and third place in the construction competition, get certificates. A separate certificate is given in each item.","In the exhibition competition (all items together), the class that gets the most points gets the first place certificate of the exhibition competition. The class that gets the most points in the construction competition gets the first place certificate of the construction competition. The class that gets the most points in exhibition and construction together gets the first place certificate of the combined exhibition and construction competition.","At the sub-district level for HS (at most 20 items) and for HSS and VHSS (at most 20 items), the school that gets the highest points in the construction competition gets the rolling trophy. The schools that get second and third place get certificates.","The grade and points of the exhibition competition follow the same table: Grade A (80 percent or more) gives 5 points, Grade B (70 to 79 percent) gives 3 points and Grade C (60 to 69 percent) gives 1 point."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Prizes and Certificates","Items":["Competitors who get a grade receive certificates from the school level.","Winners at the sub-district and revenue district fairs get certificates and encouragement awards.","At the state fair, the first three places in each item get certificates, cash awards and honours.","At the closing ceremony of the state fair, the overall championships are given with their certificates and special honours.","The trophy committee collects the trophies of the last year, repairs and polishes them, and prepares the trophies and certificates from the list that the programme committee gives every day. They are given on the same days. Trophies and certificates not given are counted, entered in the trophy register and given to the concerned Deputy Director of Education.","The team manager or the escorting teacher signs the trophy register as clear proof of receiving the trophies.","When the competitions are over, the trophy register is completed and handed to the concerned education officer. At the state level it is handed to the PRO.","Everrolling trophies and shields last for ten years. After that, if the donors do not give new ones, the Director of General Education takes them back.","If a certificate given by the Director of General Education is lost or has errors, the head master or principal sends an application with a demand draft of {{CertificateReplacementFee}} in the name of the Director of General Education to get a new certificate."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct and Safety","Items":["The whole Kerala School Sasthrolsavam must be held strictly under the Green Protocol.","A student, teacher or other person who tries to spoil the Sasthrolsavam by shameless, undisciplined or provoking behaviour gets a proper punishment, including being made ineligible. Action by the department can also be taken.","Only items that keep the safety of the children can be held, from school level to state level. The organisers must take special care to arrange all safety measures.","The Law and Order Committee keeps discipline and order at the venue of the fair, with the help of police officers, SPC, NCC, scouts, guides, other helpful organisations and leading citizens. Police service must be there until the fair ends.","Light is arranged at all places at all times. Plug points are arranged on the stages and stalls (at least 5 power plugs in each room of the exhibition stalls), with a generator and a sound system. The certificates for electrical safety are given to the General Convener 2 days before the fair starts.","The Public Works Department gives the fitness certificate of the stages, and it goes to the General Convener 2 days before the fair starts. The fire force is arranged and a pandal is given for it.","The Welfare Committee looks after the welfare and health of the participants and officials. Medical help and first aid are available at all times with the Public Health Department. Cleaning of the place of stay, the competition places, the food halls and the surroundings is arranged with the local self government department. Drinking water must be there everywhere.","The Green Protocol Committee has the Suchitwa Mission district coordinator as its chairman, gives directions to keep the stages and the surroundings clean and green, gives awareness of the Green Protocol to the competitors and the viewers, and gives guidelines to avoid plastic."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judges and Judging","Items":["Judges are fair, well known and capable persons. When judges are chosen, their bio data and declaration are taken in writing, as in the annexure. At every level at least three judges must be there to judge.","A person cannot be a judge in the science fairs and the related competitions for more than two years. A sub-district judge cannot be a judge at the revenue district fair of the same revenue district. A district level judge cannot be a judge at the state Sasthrolsavam or its related competitions in the same year.","Every year the Director of General Education chooses the state and district judges from the nominations of persons from the Government institutions of the state, the Government recognised education institutions, experts in the subjects and persons in higher education, after a careful check. The Deputy Directors of Education are responsible for choosing the sub-district judges by the same standard.","The programme committee gives the judges the score sheets and the remark sheets in time, and collects and keeps their bio data and declaration.","The score sheet with the evaluation indicators gets the approval of the General Convener.","There must be no cutting or correction on a score sheet. If a correction cannot be avoided, the person who evaluated must sign it fully at the place.","A judge gives an evaluation note, with an opinion, for each child along with the score sheet.","After each competition the score sheet, the remark sheet, the tabulation sheet and the report of the stage manager are collected. The points are written on the score board in time.","The mark lists of the competitions and the tabulation sheets of the results are sealed and kept for one year in the office of the sub-district education officer (or the Deputy Director of Education at revenue district level). They are produced when the appeal committee or higher officers ask for them.","The programme committee prepares the results and uploads them, and gives the results to the trophy committee and the publicity committee in time. It prepares, with the Kite, the list of winners for the higher level competitions and gives it to the upper levels.","All item competitions are recorded on video, and a CD is prepared to help the appeal committee study the complaints. For on-the-spot competitions the video is recorded when the products are finished. The programme committee is responsible for this.","The same four marks apply to every item of the on-the-spot construction competition, in every section: workload in making the product and the part of the child, 40 percent; skill and completeness in making the product, 25 percent; knowledge of the raw materials and tools used to make the product, 20 percent; social use, speciality and marketability of the product, 15 percent.","Exhibition competition marks (10 in all): arrangement of the products for the exhibition, 50 percent (5 marks); knowledge of the marketing possibility, price and presentation, 30 percent (3 marks, by viva); knowledge of the social use of the product and presentation, 20 percent (2 marks, by viva).","Judges also hold a viva in some items (for example Book Binding)."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Complaints and Appeals","Items":["An appeal committee must be formed at every level to give judgment on complaints about the results of the Science, Maths, Social Science, Work Experience and IT fairs.","The appeal committees consider appeals on the basis of the judgments of the Honourable High Court on this matter and the rules in the manual. The decision of the appeal committee is final.","A complaint must be given to the appeal committee within one hour after the result is announced. An appeal given after one hour is not accepted for any reason.","The appeal committee studies the complaints clearly, gives its decision and issues the order of action on the appeal in the format of the annexure.","There is no appeal fee at the school level. The appeal fee is {{AppealFeeSubDistrict}} at the sub-district level, {{AppealFeeRevenueDistrict}} at the revenue district level, {{AppealFeeState}} at the state level and {{AppealFeeHigher}} for a higher appeal.","If the decision is in favour of the appeal, the appeal fee is given back. If not, the amount is added to the fund of the organising committee.","The school level appeal committee has the principal or head master and the coordinators of the school science, maths, social science, work experience and IT clubs (one representative of each). Only the competitor who got first place with an A grade at the school level can go to the sub-district fair. The appeal committee confirms this at the time of the appeal check.","The sub-district appeal committee has the District Education Officer as chairman, the sub-district education officer as vice chairman, one representative each of the RDD and the AD, the General Convener and one expert in the subject. Complaints go through the escorting teacher, in the fixed form, with the fixed fee, within one hour after the result is announced. Only complaints given through the escorting teacher are considered.","The revenue district appeal committee has the Deputy Director of Education as chairman, the RDD or AD as vice chairman, the District Education Officer, the Kite district coordinator and an expert or the regional foreman in the subject. Complaints go through the team manager, in the fixed form, with the fixed fee. Only complaints given through the team manager are considered.","The state appeal committee has the Director of General Education as chairman, the Additional Director (Academic) as vice chairman, the Director of Higher Secondary Education, the Director of Vocational Higher Secondary Education, the vice chairman and executive director of Kite, and an expert in the subject. Complaints go through the revenue district team manager or joint team manager, in the fixed form with the fixed fee. Only complaints given through the team manager are considered.","A competitor who goes to a higher level because of a court order or an order of an appeal authority is counted as a participant.","The members of the appeal committee and the judges give a declaration in the format of the annexure."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Other Parts of the Manual","Items":["This page covers the Work Experience Fair only. The Sasthrolsavam also has the Science Fair, Maths Fair, Social Science Fair, IT Fair. Each has its own page.","The manual also holds the Kerala School Skill Festival for the students of the Vocational Higher Secondary courses, with its own manual part. It is held along with the Sasthrolsavam and is not covered here.","The manual has annexures: the entry forms for each fair and level, the evaluation sheets, a regional list of VHS schools, the format of the identity card for a child, the declaration for judges and appeal committee members, the application form for an appeal and the format of the appeal order.","The Programme Committee of the state fair keeps the competitor lists, score sheets, time sheets, tabulation sheets and score boards, gives the code numbers and a leaflet of instructions, and appoints and names teachers for the smooth running of the competitions. It also gives notices on the stages and keeps the time of every competition as planned. It sees to the internet and wi-fi, computers and equipment at each place, and the printing of certificates and the uploading of results.","The Reception Committee makes the list of persons to be invited to the opening and the closing, invites the guests, prints and gives invitations with the approval of the protocol officer, and receives the guests, the judges and the teams that come from the districts.","The Exhibition and Cultural Committee makes all the facilities for the exhibition (with the evaluation committee) at the venue school, keeps the exhibits from the districts safe, arranges facilities for judges to evaluate at the stalls, and lets the students and the public visit all stalls. It also gives code numbers and stall numbers for each district and arranges cultural programmes after the exhibition time.","The Food Committee gives food to the students, teachers, guests, judges, officials, organising committee members, volunteers and media persons. On the evaluation day food is given at the stalls. The special food items needed by the competitors of the on-the-spot competitions must be given at the competition place.","The Pandal and Stage Committee builds the pandals for the on-the-spot competitions and the exhibition stalls, with separate stalls for each section of each district, and separate stalls for the Primary, HS, HSS and VHSS teaching aids and teacher projects, for the Work Experience on-the-spot competitions and for the exhibition. It also builds the pandals for the opening and the closing, with toilets and urinals, chairs and furniture.","The Publicity Committee gives publicity for all the matters of the Sasthrolsavam in audio, visual and print media, banners and arches, and makes sure the competition results from the Programme Committee reach the news media in time.","The Accommodation Committee decides the place of stay for the teams that have completed registration, and arranges water, light, bathrooms and toilets. The stay of the judges, the officials and the committee convenors at the state fair is kept with the Public Relations Officer of the Directorate of General Education.","The Transport Committee arranges vehicles for the teams and guests that come to the fair, and asks the railway, the State Transport, the private bus owners and the school buses for special services to the venue and back.","The Souvenir Committee prepares and publishes the Sasthrolsavam Souvenir (Sasthrolsava Rekha). It collects articles, photos and advertisements with the approval of the General Convener, takes advertisement amounts at the tariff rate, bears the cost of the publication, gives the Souvenir with details and pictures to the General Convener within one month after the fair, and sends copies to the District Education Offices and the Higher Secondary and Vocational Higher Secondary Directorates.","The manual also prints the Work Experience Fair rules for Special School students: they have their own competitions at the state fair, held together with this fair.","The manual also lists the Work Experience items of the Special Schools and the evaluation sheet of the on-the-spot competition in the annexures."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"Kerala School Sasthrolsavam Manual 2025 (PDF)","Url":"https://mela.kite.kerala.gov.in/2026/entry_forms/sasthrolsavam_manual_2025.pdf"},{"Title":"Kerala School Sasthrolsavam Item List 2026 (KITE)","Url":"https://mela.kite.kerala.gov.in/2026/index.php/Home/item_list"}]}'),o=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.9 A, pp.123-124",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Every item of the Work Experience Fair is for one child. A competitor can take part in only one item of the on-the-spot construction competition.","A competitor of the on-the-spot competition must also take part in the exhibition competition."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Every item of the Work Experience Fair is for one child. A competitor can take part in only one item of the on-the-spot construction competition.
- A competitor of the on-the-spot competition must also take part in the exhibition competition.`}],a=[{AgeGroup:"WorkExp LP",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.9 A 1(a), p.123 and Annexure 1, pp.130-131",Sections:{About:["The LP section is for children of classes 1 to 4."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["At the school level the items of Annexure 1 are held as on-the-spot construction competitions and exhibition competitions. The 25 items are Agarbathi Making, Bamboo Products, Beads Work, Book Binding, Coconut Shell Products, Coir Door Mats, Electrical Wiring, Embroidery, Fabric Painting, Fabric Printing Using Vegetables, Metal Engraving, Modelling with Clay, Origami, Paper Craft, Pottery Painting, Poster Designing, Prepare Pattern Using Threads, Product Using Card and Straw Board, Products Using Waste Materials, Puppet Making, Sheet Metal Work, Stuffed Toys, Umbrella Making, Wood Carving and Wood Work.","The competition ends at the sub-district level, where there is no exhibition.","At the sub-district level a school can take part in at most 10 items in LP."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- The LP section is for children of classes 1 to 4.

## Rules
- At the school level the items of Annexure 1 are held as on-the-spot construction competitions and exhibition competitions. The 25 items are Agarbathi Making, Bamboo Products, Beads Work, Book Binding, Coconut Shell Products, Coir Door Mats, Electrical Wiring, Embroidery, Fabric Painting, Fabric Printing Using Vegetables, Metal Engraving, Modelling with Clay, Origami, Paper Craft, Pottery Painting, Poster Designing, Prepare Pattern Using Threads, Product Using Card and Straw Board, Products Using Waste Materials, Puppet Making, Sheet Metal Work, Stuffed Toys, Umbrella Making, Wood Carving and Wood Work.
- The competition ends at the sub-district level, where there is no exhibition.
- At the sub-district level a school can take part in at most 10 items in LP.`},{AgeGroup:"WorkExp UP",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.9 A 1(a), p.123 and Annexure 1, pp.130-131",Sections:{About:["The UP section is for children of classes 5 to 7."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The UP section holds the same 25 items as the LP section (Annexure 1).","The competition ends at the sub-district level, where there is no exhibition.","At the sub-district level a school can take part in at most 10 items in UP."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- The UP section is for children of classes 5 to 7.

## Rules
- The UP section holds the same 25 items as the LP section (Annexure 1).
- The competition ends at the sub-district level, where there is no exhibition.
- At the sub-district level a school can take part in at most 10 items in UP.`},{AgeGroup:"WorkExp HS",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.9 A 1(b), p.123 and Annexure 2, pp.132-134",Sections:{About:["The HS section is for children of classes 8 to 10."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The 35 items of Annexure 2 are held as on-the-spot construction competitions and exhibition competitions.","The competition goes up to the state level.","At the sub-district level a school can take part in at most 20 items in HS."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- The HS section is for children of classes 8 to 10.

## Rules
- The 35 items of Annexure 2 are held as on-the-spot construction competitions and exhibition competitions.
- The competition goes up to the state level.
- At the sub-district level a school can take part in at most 20 items in HS.`},{AgeGroup:"WExp HSS/VHSS",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.9 A 1(b), p.123 and Annexure 2, pp.132-134",Sections:{About:["The HSS and VHSS section is for children of classes 11 and 12."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The 35 items of Annexure 2 are held as on-the-spot construction competitions and exhibition competitions.","The competition goes up to the state level.","At the sub-district level a school can take part in at most 20 items in HSS and VHSS."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- The HSS and VHSS section is for children of classes 11 and 12.

## Rules
- The 35 items of Annexure 2 are held as on-the-spot construction competitions and exhibition competitions.
- The competition goes up to the state level.
- At the sub-district level a school can take part in at most 20 items in HSS and VHSS.`}],i=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Agarbathi Making","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 1, p.135","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for LP and UP only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Bring all the powders needed to make the sticks in separate packets, the essences, and the oils for fixing in separate bottles. The sticks can be brought coloured.","The masala dough (koottu) is made at the competition place.","The child must know about the chemicals (lines) used to give the smell.","The covers to pack the sticks and the boxes are made at the competition place.","Furniture is not allowed. Bring the board needed for making.","The ratio of the colour of the stick to the colour of the incense must be exact. A thick difference in the gap is not allowed. The top of the incense must not show the stick."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges check the method of making the stick using bamboo or reed, the masala compound and the lines, and the child's knowledge of them.","The quality, the number and the value of the incense sticks the child makes are considered."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for LP and UP only.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Bring all the powders needed to make the sticks in separate packets, the essences, and the oils for fixing in separate bottles. The sticks can be brought coloured.\\n- The masala dough (koottu) is made at the competition place.\\n- The child must know about the chemicals (lines) used to give the smell.\\n- The covers to pack the sticks and the boxes are made at the competition place.\\n- Furniture is not allowed. Bring the board needed for making.\\n- The ratio of the colour of the stick to the colour of the incense must be exact. A thick difference in the gap is not allowed. The top of the incense must not show the stick.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges check the method of making the stick using bamboo or reed, the masala compound and the lines, and the child's knowledge of them.\\n- The quality, the number and the value of the incense sticks the child makes are considered."},{"Title":"Bamboo Products","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 2, p.136 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 1, p.145","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Bamboo or reed strips are made and brought to the competition place.","The products made must be useful, strong, and finished within the fixed time.","The strips can be coloured."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The skill of the child, the variety of the products and the use are considered in the evaluation."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Bamboo or reed strips are made and brought to the competition place.\\n- The products made must be useful, strong, and finished within the fixed time.\\n- The strips can be coloured.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The skill of the child, the variety of the products and the use are considered in the evaluation."},{"Title":"Beads Work","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 3, p.136 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 2, p.145","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make different kinds of ornaments with beads. Plastic beads or other kinds of beads can be used.","Make only the designs and items that the judges give."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["A good model, the combination of colours and skill are given special consideration."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Make different kinds of ornaments with beads. Plastic beads or other kinds of beads can be used.\\n- Make only the designs and items that the judges give.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- A good model, the combination of colours and skill are given special consideration."},{"Title":"Book Binding","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 4, pp.136-137 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 3, p.145","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Bring full scap (43.18 cm x 34.29 cm) or demy (44.45 cm x 55.88 cm) paper, calico, straw board, chart card and fancy paper, and all materials and tools needed to make the book.","The paper that the judges approve is in every book.","The judges hold an oral test (viva) too."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges judge using different binding methods (half bound, quarter bound), the different books, the number of sections, the pages, the size, the different stitching methods and the number of books."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Bring full scap (43.18 cm x 34.29 cm) or demy (44.45 cm x 55.88 cm) paper, calico, straw board, chart card and fancy paper, and all materials and tools needed to make the book.\\n- The paper that the judges approve is in every book.\\n- The judges hold an oral test (viva) too.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges judge using different binding methods (half bound, quarter bound), the different books, the number of sections, the pages, the size, the different stitching methods and the number of books."},{"Title":"Coconut Shell Products","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 5, p.137 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 4-5, p.146","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Removing the hair of the shell, smoothing, cutting and polishing are done at the competition place.","Electrical machines must not be used in making.","Make the products that the judges direct."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The completeness of the products, the child's effort, the skill, the accuracy and the delicacy are considered."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Removing the hair of the shell, smoothing, cutting and polishing are done at the competition place.\\n- Electrical machines must not be used in making.\\n- Make the products that the judges direct.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The completeness of the products, the child's effort, the skill, the accuracy and the delicacy are considered."},{"Title":"Coir Door Mats","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 6, p.137 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 6, p.146","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Bring coir, plain or coloured, the frame and the other tools to the competition place.","A mat made using a frame gets priority in marks.","Make as many mats as can be finished in 3 hours."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Bring coir, plain or coloured, the frame and the other tools to the competition place.\\n- A mat made using a frame gets priority in marks.\\n- Make as many mats as can be finished in 3 hours."},{"Title":"Electrical Wiring","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 7, pp.137-138 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 10, p.148","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The child does house wiring on a board of at most 150 cm x 105 cm, using the modern electrical safety method, with a PVC open circuit system or a PVC casing and capping system, including the traditional stair case wiring. Only one board is used.","Bring the unprocessed materials and the tools. Do not mark the board or the materials beforehand, and do not make holes in them beforehand.","All connections and fixing are done at the competition place. The child draws the connection diagram in the competition and shows it.","The child must have a right understanding of the electrical wiring, the safety arrangements and the tools.","Single phase electricity is available.","Electrical machines and furniture are not allowed. The work is done on the floor."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- The child does house wiring on a board of at most 150 cm x 105 cm, using the modern electrical safety method, with a PVC open circuit system or a PVC casing and capping system, including the traditional stair case wiring. Only one board is used.\\n- Bring the unprocessed materials and the tools. Do not mark the board or the materials beforehand, and do not make holes in them beforehand.\\n- All connections and fixing are done at the competition place. The child draws the connection diagram in the competition and shows it.\\n- The child must have a right understanding of the electrical wiring, the safety arrangements and the tools.\\n- Single phase electricity is available.\\n- Electrical machines and furniture are not allowed. The work is done on the floor."},{"Title":"Embroidery","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 8, p.138 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 12, p.149","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Bring cloth large enough for a cushion cover or a pillow cover, the threads needed for stitching, a frame, scissors, carbon paper and a pencil.","Draw the design the judges give on the cloth and finish the stitching. Single layer or multi layer thread can be used.","Use stitches that suit the nature of the picture.","Only cotton cloth is allowed. Machines and mat cloth are not allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The arrangement of the stitches, the different stitches, the combination of colours, excellence and completeness are considered."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Bring cloth large enough for a cushion cover or a pillow cover, the threads needed for stitching, a frame, scissors, carbon paper and a pencil.\\n- Draw the design the judges give on the cloth and finish the stitching. Single layer or multi layer thread can be used.\\n- Use stitches that suit the nature of the picture.\\n- Only cotton cloth is allowed. Machines and mat cloth are not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The arrangement of the stitches, the different stitches, the combination of colours, excellence and completeness are considered."},{"Title":"Fabric Painting","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 9, p.138 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 13, pp.149-150","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Bring 1.25 metres of white poplin cloth, colour, brush, pencil and carbon paper.","Draw the design the judges give and finish it with colour."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The completeness of the picture, the combination of colours and accuracy are considered."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Bring 1.25 metres of white poplin cloth, colour, brush, pencil and carbon paper.\\n- Draw the design the judges give and finish it with colour.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The completeness of the picture, the combination of colours and accuracy are considered."},{"Title":"Fabric Printing Using Vegetables","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 10, pp.138-139 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 14, p.150","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Bring the poplin cloth needed, fabric paint, vegetables, a cloth and a sponge.","Only blocks made at the competition place can be used. Ready made design stamps must not be used to make the blocks."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The designs, the combination of colours, the pattern and skill are considered."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Bring the poplin cloth needed, fabric paint, vegetables, a cloth and a sponge.\\n- Only blocks made at the competition place can be used. Ready made design stamps must not be used to make the blocks.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The designs, the combination of colours, the pattern and skill are considered."},{"Title":"Metal Engraving","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 11, p.139 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 19, p.152","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The child engraves a picture on a sheet of aluminium or copper. The size of the sheet is 60 cm x 40 cm.","Marking and drawing pictures on the sheet are done at the competition place. The sheet can be brought painted and framed beforehand.","Only engraving tools can be used. The drawing for the engraving (A3 size) is given at the competition place.","Bring the aluminium sheet, pencil, pen, carbon paper and the suitable tools."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- The child engraves a picture on a sheet of aluminium or copper. The size of the sheet is 60 cm x 40 cm.\\n- Marking and drawing pictures on the sheet are done at the competition place. The sheet can be brought painted and framed beforehand.\\n- Only engraving tools can be used. The drawing for the engraving (A3 size) is given at the competition place.\\n- Bring the aluminium sheet, pencil, pen, carbon paper and the suitable tools."},{"Title":"Modelling with Clay","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 12, p.139 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 20, p.152","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Bring prepared clay and the other tools, and a 50 cm x 50 cm board or plywood.","Make the figure as the judges direct."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Bring prepared clay and the other tools, and a 50 cm x 50 cm board or plywood.\\n- Make the figure as the judges direct."},{"Title":"Origami","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 13, pp.139-140","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for LP and UP only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make forms by folding, creasing and shaping different papers many times, into complete forms.","Papers of any kind can be used: cut and uncut papers, drawing paper, map litho paper, craft paper, cover paper, varnish paper and fluorescent paper. The paper must be at most 40 cm x 40 cm.","Make at most 5 pieces in one section. Examples are birds, fish and animals.","Forms made by sticking or joining are not allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The number of times the folds are repeated, the likeness of the form, the proportional size and the number are considered."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for LP and UP only.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Make forms by folding, creasing and shaping different papers many times, into complete forms.\\n- Papers of any kind can be used: cut and uncut papers, drawing paper, map litho paper, craft paper, cover paper, varnish paper and fluorescent paper. The paper must be at most 40 cm x 40 cm.\\n- Make at most 5 pieces in one section. Examples are birds, fish and animals.\\n- Forms made by sticking or joining are not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The number of times the folds are repeated, the likeness of the form, the proportional size and the number are considered."},{"Title":"Paper Craft","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 14, p.140 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 21, pp.152-153","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make flowers, leaves and the like that look like those seen in nature, using different papers such as tissue, crepe, varnish, velvet and phoenix paper.","Paper folded and shaped aiming at one product is not allowed.","Bring the materials and the tools needed. Use simple flower vases only for the exhibition. A stand must not be used."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Make flowers, leaves and the like that look like those seen in nature, using different papers such as tissue, crepe, varnish, velvet and phoenix paper.\\n- Paper folded and shaped aiming at one product is not allowed.\\n- Bring the materials and the tools needed. Use simple flower vases only for the exhibition. A stand must not be used."},{"Title":"Pottery Painting","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 15, p.140 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 23, p.153","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The child makes products by painting with acrylic paint on different earthen pots for house decoration.","The children bring all the things needed (earthen pots, paint, brush, pencil, scale). Use earthen pots of 5 inch to 9 inch.","Moulds made beforehand and other signs must not be used. The design must have many colours.","No marking of any kind is allowed on the pots.","Make as many pieces as can be finished in 3 hours."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- The child makes products by painting with acrylic paint on different earthen pots for house decoration.\\n- The children bring all the things needed (earthen pots, paint, brush, pencil, scale). Use earthen pots of 5 inch to 9 inch.\\n- Moulds made beforehand and other signs must not be used. The design must have many colours.\\n- No marking of any kind is allowed on the pots.\\n- Make as many pieces as can be finished in 3 hours."},{"Title":"Poster Designing","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 16, pp.140-141 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 24, p.154","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Use poster colours. Make a poster on the subject the judges give, on dummy size paper.","The children bring the paper, colours and all the things needed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Use poster colours. Make a poster on the subject the judges give, on dummy size paper.\\n- The children bring the paper, colours and all the things needed."},{"Title":"Prepare Pattern Using Threads","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 17, p.141 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 22, p.153","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Bring a 40 cm x 40 cm plywood or hard board with painted paper or cloth stuck on it, without any marks.","Drawing the pattern, hammering the nails and the like are done at the competition place. The pattern is drawn on the paper the invigilator gives.","Any kind of thread can be used. Furniture is not allowed. A thermocol sheet is not allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Bring a 40 cm x 40 cm plywood or hard board with painted paper or cloth stuck on it, without any marks.\\n- Drawing the pattern, hammering the nails and the like are done at the competition place. The pattern is drawn on the paper the invigilator gives.\\n- Any kind of thread can be used. Furniture is not allowed. A thermocol sheet is not allowed."},{"Title":"Product Using Card & Straw Board","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 18, pp.141-142 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 27, pp.154-155","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make the items of the section as the section rows say, using 64 ounce or 32 ounce straw board, laced flexi file material, card board (duplex board, grey board) and an 8 ounce board box.","Card board must not be folded and brought.","Make no more than the number of products shown for each item."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Make the items of the section as the section rows say, using 64 ounce or 32 ounce straw board, laced flexi file material, card board (duplex board, grey board) and an 8 ounce board box.\\n- Card board must not be folded and brought.\\n- Make no more than the number of products shown for each item."},{"Title":"Products Using Waste Materials","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 19, p.142 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 29, pp.156-157","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make teaching aids, decoration items, and other useful low cost things from waste materials.","Made forms or other materials that are cooked or processed beforehand are not allowed.","Make at most three products each of teaching aids, craft items and items of social relevance (for example waste processing, current relevance and use in daily life). The total number of products is 9.","Products using the areca palm spathe are not allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Make teaching aids, decoration items, and other useful low cost things from waste materials.\\n- Made forms or other materials that are cooked or processed beforehand are not allowed.\\n- Make at most three products each of teaching aids, craft items and items of social relevance (for example waste processing, current relevance and use in daily life). The total number of products is 9.\\n- Products using the areca palm spathe are not allowed."},{"Title":"Puppet Making","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 20, pp.142-143 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 30, p.157","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make a string puppet and a hand puppet (glove puppet), make them work and show them.","The parts of the body are made in cloth, filled with cotton, in the right proportions. The parts of the body of a string puppet are joined so that they can move as needed.","The puppets can be decorated with attractive ornaments and with dresses made at the competition place.","The head of the hand puppet is made with light things. Holes for the fingers to go in are made.","Make a presentation that gives a social and current message, without a stage.","Parts or clothes made beforehand are not allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Make a string puppet and a hand puppet (glove puppet), make them work and show them.\\n- The parts of the body are made in cloth, filled with cotton, in the right proportions. The parts of the body of a string puppet are joined so that they can move as needed.\\n- The puppets can be decorated with attractive ornaments and with dresses made at the competition place.\\n- The head of the hand puppet is made with light things. Holes for the fingers to go in are made.\\n- Make a presentation that gives a social and current message, without a stage.\\n- Parts or clothes made beforehand are not allowed."},{"Title":"Sheet Metal Work","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 21, p.143 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 32, p.158","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make products for daily use with 22 SWG or 24 SWG sheet metal.","Marking, cutting and bending are done at the competition place.","Join by riveting, soldering and hemming methods."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The use of the products, skill in the work and quality are considered."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Make products for daily use with 22 SWG or 24 SWG sheet metal.\\n- Marking, cutting and bending are done at the competition place.\\n- Join by riveting, soldering and hemming methods.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The use of the products, skill in the work and quality are considered."},{"Title":"Stuffed Toys","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 22, p.143 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 33, p.158","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Draw the forms of animals and birds on cloth, cut them out, stitch them like a mould, and fill them with soft materials to make toys.","Different pieces of cloth can be joined, and the eyes, nose and ears can be stitched on.","Drawing the pattern, cutting and stitching are done at the competition place."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Draw the forms of animals and birds on cloth, cut them out, stitch them like a mould, and fill them with soft materials to make toys.\\n- Different pieces of cloth can be joined, and the eyes, nose and ears can be stitched on.\\n- Drawing the pattern, cutting and stitching are done at the competition place."},{"Title":"Umbrella Making","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 23, p.143","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for LP and UP only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make one ladies' umbrella and one gents' umbrella, and other modern umbrellas that can be folded.","Folding the tube to shape, fixing the nails, tying and fixing the rods, cutting and stitching the cloth and joining are done at the competition place.","As many umbrellas as possible can be made in this way. A frame made beforehand by tying rods must not be brought."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for LP and UP only.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Make one ladies' umbrella and one gents' umbrella, and other modern umbrellas that can be folded.\\n- Folding the tube to shape, fixing the nails, tying and fixing the rods, cutting and stitching the cloth and joining are done at the competition place.\\n- As many umbrellas as possible can be made in this way. A frame made beforehand by tying rods must not be brought."},{"Title":"Wood Carving","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 24, pp.143-144 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 34, p.158-159","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The aim is carving work on a 40 cm x 40 cm board.","Marking, drawing and all other work are done at the competition place only.","Use suitable carving tools. Use the drawings the judges give. Electric tools are not allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- The aim is carving work on a 40 cm x 40 cm board.\\n- Marking, drawing and all other work are done at the competition place only.\\n- Use suitable carving tools. Use the drawings the judges give. Electric tools are not allowed."},{"Title":"Wood Work","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 25, p.144 and Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 35, p.159","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make any item that can be used.","The children cut, chisel, mark and make holes in the blocks they bring, as needed, all at the competition place.","Use proper joints to join the parts. Electrical tools are not allowed in the making."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Make any item that can be used.\\n- The children cut, chisel, mark and make holes in the blocks they bring, as needed, all at the competition place.\\n- Use proper joints to join the parts. Electrical tools are not allowed in the making."},{"Title":"Different Types of Carry Bags","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 8, p.147","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make different kinds of bags for daily use, from cloth and paper. Attractive bags of different sizes can be made."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Make different kinds of bags for daily use, from cloth and paper. Attractive bags of different sizes can be made."},{"Title":"Budding, Layering, Grafting etc.","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 4, p.146","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only. It covers budding, layering, grafting and the like."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Bring suitable stems and creepers of different plants (for example rubber, mango, guava, sapota, nutmeg, jasmine and chilli) and the tools.","Do and show 3 of each type. A total of 3 made earlier can be shown for each type.","A nursery display is not allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only. It covers budding, layering, grafting and the like.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Bring suitable stems and creepers of different plants (for example rubber, mango, guava, sapota, nutmeg, jasmine and chilli) and the tools.\\n- Do and show 3 of each type. A total of 3 made earlier can be shown for each type.\\n- A nursery display is not allowed."},{"Title":"Doll Making","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 7, pp.146-147","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make attractive dolls in human shape for a special purpose (for example dance forms, or dolls in different dresses).","Bend thin wire (about 1 mm thick) in the proportion of the body to make the skeleton, put cotton on it and wind woollen thread round it to form the body parts.","Make the attractive dress at the competition place and decorate the doll with ornaments. The doll can be at most 35 cm high.","All making is done at the competition place. Parts made beforehand are not allowed.","Bring the wooden heads, cloth and lace needed. A Kathakali crown and a Theyyam costume are not allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Make attractive dolls in human shape for a special purpose (for example dance forms, or dolls in different dresses).\\n- Bend thin wire (about 1 mm thick) in the proportion of the body to make the skeleton, put cotton on it and wind woollen thread round it to form the body parts.\\n- Make the attractive dress at the competition place and decorate the doll with ornaments. The doll can be at most 35 cm high.\\n- All making is done at the competition place. Parts made beforehand are not allowed.\\n- Bring the wooden heads, cloth and lace needed. A Kathakali crown and a Theyyam costume are not allowed."},{"Title":"Economic Nutritious Food Items and Vegetable Fruit Preservation Items","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 9, pp.147-148","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only. It has two parts: economic nutritious food items, and vegetable and fruit preservation items."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Economic nutritious food items are low cost, easily got from the surroundings and rich in nutrition. The same material must not be repeated to make many dishes. The dishes must be balanced nutrition dishes with grain, protein, fat, vitamins and minerals. Make and show at most 6 dishes.","Preservation items: make pickles, sauces, squash and jam from vegetables, fruits and the like, using the vegetables and fruits easily got from the surroundings. Quantities: pickle 250 gm, jam 250 gm, sauce 250 gm and squash 750 ml. Make and show at most 6 items.","In all, 12 dishes and items at most (both parts together).","Bring the unprocessed materials, the small tools, the utensils and the vessels. Items made beforehand are not allowed.","Only a kerosene wick stove is allowed. Induction cookers and pressure cookers are not allowed.","The quantity of a cooked dish is about 200 to 300 gm.","Only two desks and one bench are allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Cleanliness, the ability to work, the cooking methods, ways that do not lose nutrition, quality, and the display of the dishes are considered."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only. It has two parts: economic nutritious food items, and vegetable and fruit preservation items.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Economic nutritious food items are low cost, easily got from the surroundings and rich in nutrition. The same material must not be repeated to make many dishes. The dishes must be balanced nutrition dishes with grain, protein, fat, vitamins and minerals. Make and show at most 6 dishes.\\n- Preservation items: make pickles, sauces, squash and jam from vegetables, fruits and the like, using the vegetables and fruits easily got from the surroundings. Quantities: pickle 250 gm, jam 250 gm, sauce 250 gm and squash 750 ml. Make and show at most 6 items.\\n- In all, 12 dishes and items at most (both parts together).\\n- Bring the unprocessed materials, the small tools, the utensils and the vessels. Items made beforehand are not allowed.\\n- Only a kerosene wick stove is allowed. Induction cookers and pressure cookers are not allowed.\\n- The quantity of a cooked dish is about 200 to 300 gm.\\n- Only two desks and one bench are allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Cleanliness, the ability to work, the cooking methods, ways that do not lose nutrition, quality, and the display of the dishes are considered."},{"Title":"Electronics","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 11, p.149","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The work aims at products that can be used and that work.","The circuit diagram is drawn and brought to the competition.","The child must have a clear idea of the different parts used and the equipment. Make and show at most 10 products.","Parts joined beforehand are not allowed. Single phase electricity is available at the competition place.","Only a multi purpose PCB can be used. A bread board must not be used. Different kinds of sensors can be included."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The working of the product and the skill in making are valued."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The work aims at products that can be used and that work.\\n- The circuit diagram is drawn and brought to the competition.\\n- The child must have a clear idea of the different parts used and the equipment. Make and show at most 10 products.\\n- Parts joined beforehand are not allowed. Single phase electricity is available at the competition place.\\n- Only a multi purpose PCB can be used. A bread board must not be used. Different kinds of sensors can be included.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The working of the product and the skill in making are valued."},{"Title":"Fabrication Using Fibre","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 15, p.150","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Using fibre or PVC materials (door materials, panels and so on), make a cabin door of 80 cm height and 60 cm width with a frame and fit the fittings.","Besides, daily use products can be made with the same materials.","Material must not be cut to exact size and brought. The needed sizes are marked and cut at the competition place.","The competitors bring all the things needed. Electric tools are not allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Using fibre or PVC materials (door materials, panels and so on), make a cabin door of 80 cm height and 60 cm width with a frame and fit the fittings.\\n- Besides, daily use products can be made with the same materials.\\n- Material must not be cut to exact size and brought. The needed sizes are marked and cut at the competition place.\\n- The competitors bring all the things needed. Electric tools are not allowed."},{"Title":"Garment Making","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 16, p.151","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Bring the cloth, needle, thread, lace, tape, scale, pencil and all other things needed.","Stitch the garments by hand as the question that the judges give says."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Bring the cloth, needle, thread, lace, tape, scale, pencil and all other things needed.\\n- Stitch the garments by hand as the question that the judges give says."},{"Title":"Innovative Working Model","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 17, p.151","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Put new ideas of the present time into daily life. Using different materials that suit nature, electrical, electronic and mechanical parts and different sensors, build a working model of a product that is useful in daily life and makes human life easy. The child shows creativity and skill in making.","The competitor brings the materials for making. Devices that were joined beforehand are not allowed.","After the making is finished, the product is made to work in front of the judges and explained."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Put new ideas of the present time into daily life. Using different materials that suit nature, electrical, electronic and mechanical parts and different sensors, build a working model of a product that is useful in daily life and makes human life easy. The child shows creativity and skill in making.\\n- The competitor brings the materials for making. Devices that were joined beforehand are not allowed.\\n- After the making is finished, the product is made to work in front of the judges and explained."},{"Title":"Metal Embossing","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 18, pp.151-152","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Emboss pictures on a 28 gauge aluminium sheet. The size of the sheet is 30 cm x 25 cm.","Drawing and marking on the sheet are done at the competition place. The line drawing for the embossing is given at the competition place.","Bring the 28 gauge aluminium sheet, the tools, a pencil, a pen and carbon paper. Electric tools are not allowed. A tester can be used for the surroundings of the picture."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Emboss pictures on a 28 gauge aluminium sheet. The size of the sheet is 30 cm x 25 cm.\\n- Drawing and marking on the sheet are done at the competition place. The line drawing for the embossing is given at the competition place.\\n- Bring the 28 gauge aluminium sheet, the tools, a pencil, a pen and carbon paper. Electric tools are not allowed. A tester can be used for the surroundings of the picture."},{"Title":"Products Using Areca Tree Leaf","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 25, p.154","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make useful products and attractive articles using the spathe of the areca palm.","The spathes are brought flattened (levelled). Green spathes and dried spathes can be brought. Colour can be given.","The related materials needed for making (glue, rivet, thread and wooden reapers) can be used."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The shape of the product, grace, beauty, completeness and the quality of the related materials are valued."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Make useful products and attractive articles using the spathe of the areca palm.\\n- The spathes are brought flattened (levelled). Green spathes and dried spathes can be brought. Colour can be given.\\n- The related materials needed for making (glue, rivet, thread and wooden reapers) can be used.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The shape of the product, grace, beauty, completeness and the quality of the related materials are valued."},{"Title":"Products Using Natural Fiber Except Coconut Fiber","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 26, pp.154-155","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Only fibres got naturally can be used. Natural fibres, plain or coloured, are brought. The fibres must not be plaited and brought.","Make the products that the judges direct, in the size they say. Examples are a bag, a pouch, a hat and a table mat. The products must be usable.","Any one type of fibre can be used. The child must show the method of taking out the fibre and must know the process of giving colour."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only fibres got naturally can be used. Natural fibres, plain or coloured, are brought. The fibres must not be plaited and brought.\\n- Make the products that the judges direct, in the size they say. Examples are a bag, a pouch, a hat and a table mat. The products must be usable.\\n- Any one type of fibre can be used. The child must show the method of taking out the fibre and must know the process of giving colour."},{"Title":"Products Using Rexin, Canvas & Leather","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 28, p.156","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["All parts of the products to be made are cut and shaped at the competition place. Parts or materials that were made or shaped beforehand are not allowed.","Make useful products such as different kinds of bags, slippers, hats and purses. Bring the unprocessed materials and the tools needed.","Make the products in the size and shape the judges give, and finish them by hand stitching with back stitch."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The accuracy, completeness, grace, use and number of the products are considered."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- All parts of the products to be made are cut and shaped at the competition place. Parts or materials that were made or shaped beforehand are not allowed.\\n- Make useful products such as different kinds of bags, slippers, hats and purses. Bring the unprocessed materials and the tools needed.\\n- Make the products in the size and shape the judges give, and finish them by hand stitching with back stitch.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The accuracy, completeness, grace, use and number of the products are considered."},{"Title":"Ratton Work","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 31, pp.157-158","Sections":{"About":["This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only. The manual spells the item Ratton Work."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make useful products using rattan. The rattan is brought with the peel removed, bent as needed for making, or otherwise.","The products made must be such as can be finished within 3 hours. After the products are made, varnish can be put on them for grace."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This item is held for HS and HSS/VHSS only. The manual spells the item Ratton Work.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Make useful products using rattan. The rattan is brought with the peel removed, bent as needed for making, or otherwise.\\n- The products made must be such as can be finished within 3 hours. After the products are made, varnish can be put on them for grace."}]`),s=JSON.parse('[{"Title":"Book Binding","AgeGroup":"WorkExp LP","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 4, p.137","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make one notebook each in the three ways: half bound, quarter bound and drawn on cover."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Make one notebook each in the three ways: half bound, quarter bound and drawn on cover."},{"Title":"Book Binding","AgeGroup":"WorkExp UP","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 4, p.137","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make one notebook and one letter pad each in the three ways: half bound, quarter bound and drawn on cover."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Make one notebook and one letter pad each in the three ways: half bound, quarter bound and drawn on cover."},{"Title":"Book Binding","AgeGroup":"WorkExp HS","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 3, p.145","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Different books are made: a ledger, a note book, a drawn on cover book and a letter pad."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Different books are made: a ledger, a note book, a drawn on cover book and a letter pad."},{"Title":"Book Binding","AgeGroup":"WExp HSS/VHSS","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 3, p.145","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Different books are made: a ledger, a note book, a drawn on cover book and a letter pad."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Different books are made: a ledger, a note book, a drawn on cover book and a letter pad."},{"Title":"Coir Door Mats","AgeGroup":"WorkExp LP","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 6, p.137","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["LP children cannot use a frame."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Not allowed\\n- LP children cannot use a frame."},{"Title":"Fabric Printing Using Vegetables","AgeGroup":"WorkExp LP","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 10, p.138","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Print one pillow cover (75 cm x 50 cm) and one table cloth (100 cm x 100 cm)."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Print one pillow cover (75 cm x 50 cm) and one table cloth (100 cm x 100 cm)."},{"Title":"Fabric Printing Using Vegetables","AgeGroup":"WorkExp UP","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 10, p.138","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Print two pillow covers (75 cm x 50 cm) and one single bed sheet (120 cm x 210 cm)."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Print two pillow covers (75 cm x 50 cm) and one single bed sheet (120 cm x 210 cm)."},{"Title":"Fabric Printing Using Vegetables","AgeGroup":"WorkExp HS","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 14, p.150","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Print one saree and one single bed sheet (120 cm x 210 cm)."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Print one saree and one single bed sheet (120 cm x 210 cm)."},{"Title":"Fabric Printing Using Vegetables","AgeGroup":"WExp HSS/VHSS","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 14, p.150","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Print one saree, one single bed sheet (120 cm x 210 cm) and one pillow cover (75 cm x 50 cm)."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Print one saree, one single bed sheet (120 cm x 210 cm) and one pillow cover (75 cm x 50 cm)."},{"Title":"Prepare Pattern Using Threads","AgeGroup":"WorkExp LP","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 17, p.141","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["At most 3 boards are enough."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- At most 3 boards are enough."},{"Title":"Prepare Pattern Using Threads","AgeGroup":"WorkExp UP","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 17, p.141","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["At most 4 boards are enough."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- At most 4 boards are enough."},{"Title":"Prepare Pattern Using Threads","AgeGroup":"WorkExp HS","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 22, p.153","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["At most 6 boards are enough."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- At most 6 boards are enough."},{"Title":"Prepare Pattern Using Threads","AgeGroup":"WExp HSS/VHSS","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 22, p.153","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["At most 6 boards are enough."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- At most 6 boards are enough."},{"Title":"Product Using Card & Straw Board","AgeGroup":"WorkExp LP","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 18, pp.141-142","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make a writing board (1), an office file (1) and a flexi file (1).","Writing board: use 64 ounce straw board to make a writing board of 65 cm x 39 cm (two 32 ounce boards can be folded and stuck together).","Office file: use 32 ounce straw board and make the board 32 cm x 23 cm. It can be brought folded as 65 cm x 46 cm, but not folded to 32 cm x 23 cm. The flap is 60 cm long and 10 cm wide.","Flexi file: make it laced, at 35 cm x 25 cm. Card board such as duplex board and grey board can be used. Card must not be folded and brought."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Make a writing board (1), an office file (1) and a flexi file (1).\\n- Writing board: use 64 ounce straw board to make a writing board of 65 cm x 39 cm (two 32 ounce boards can be folded and stuck together).\\n- Office file: use 32 ounce straw board and make the board 32 cm x 23 cm. It can be brought folded as 65 cm x 46 cm, but not folded to 32 cm x 23 cm. The flap is 60 cm long and 10 cm wide.\\n- Flexi file: make it laced, at 35 cm x 25 cm. Card board such as duplex board and grey board can be used. Card must not be folded and brought."},{"Title":"Product Using Card & Straw Board","AgeGroup":"WorkExp UP","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 18, pp.141-142","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make 2 writing boards, 2 office files, 2 flexi files and 1 box of 8 ounce straw board (the size is given at the competition).","Writing board: 64 ounce straw board, 65 cm x 39 cm (two 32 ounce boards can be folded and stuck together).","Office file: 32 ounce straw board, 32 cm x 23 cm; it can be brought folded as 65 cm x 46 cm but not folded to 32 cm x 23 cm. The flap is 60 cm long and 10 cm wide.","Flexi file: laced, 35 cm x 25 cm. Duplex board and grey board can be used. Card must not be folded and brought.","Box: make it using 8 ounce board. The size is given at the competition."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Make 2 writing boards, 2 office files, 2 flexi files and 1 box of 8 ounce straw board (the size is given at the competition).\\n- Writing board: 64 ounce straw board, 65 cm x 39 cm (two 32 ounce boards can be folded and stuck together).\\n- Office file: 32 ounce straw board, 32 cm x 23 cm; it can be brought folded as 65 cm x 46 cm but not folded to 32 cm x 23 cm. The flap is 60 cm long and 10 cm wide.\\n- Flexi file: laced, 35 cm x 25 cm. Duplex board and grey board can be used. Card must not be folded and brought.\\n- Box: make it using 8 ounce board. The size is given at the competition."},{"Title":"Product Using Card & Straw Board","AgeGroup":"WorkExp HS","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 27, p.155","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make 3 writing boards, 3 office files, 3 flexi files, 1 box of 8 ounce straw board and 3 geometrical shapes.","The sizes of the writing board, the office file, the flexi file and the box are as given for the LP and UP sections."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Make 3 writing boards, 3 office files, 3 flexi files, 1 box of 8 ounce straw board and 3 geometrical shapes.\\n- The sizes of the writing board, the office file, the flexi file and the box are as given for the LP and UP sections."},{"Title":"Product Using Card & Straw Board","AgeGroup":"WExp HSS/VHSS","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 2(A), pp.145-159 27, p.155","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make 3 writing boards, 4 office files, 3 flexi files, 1 box of 8 ounce straw board and 3 geometrical shapes.","The sizes of the writing board, the office file, the flexi file and the box are as given for the LP and UP sections."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Make 3 writing boards, 4 office files, 3 flexi files, 1 box of 8 ounce straw board and 3 geometrical shapes.\\n- The sizes of the writing board, the office file, the flexi file and the box are as given for the LP and UP sections."},{"Title":"Puppet Making","AgeGroup":"WorkExp LP","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 20, p.143","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make 2 hand puppets."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Make 2 hand puppets."},{"Title":"Puppet Making","AgeGroup":"WorkExp UP","Source":"Manual 2025 Ch.9 Annexure 1(A), pp.135-144 20, p.143","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Make hand puppets and string puppets."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Make hand puppets and string puppets."}]'),r=[{Key:"SubDistrictRegistrationFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Registration fee at the sub-district fair",Value:"Rs. 20 per child, collected only from children of classes 9, 10, 11 and 12",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.2 B 7(b), p.12"},{Key:"AppealFeeSubDistrict",Kind:"fee",Label:"Appeal fee, sub-district level",Value:"Rs. 1000 per appeal",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.4 A, p.30 and C, p.32"},{Key:"AppealFeeRevenueDistrict",Kind:"fee",Label:"Appeal fee, revenue district level",Value:"Rs. 1500 per appeal",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.4 A, p.30 and D, p.32"},{Key:"AppealFeeState",Kind:"fee",Label:"Appeal fee, state level",Value:"Rs. 2000 per appeal",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.4 A, p.30 and E, p.33"},{Key:"AppealFeeHigher",Kind:"fee",Label:"Appeal fee, higher appeal",Value:"Rs. 2500 per appeal",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.4 A, p.30"},{Key:"CertificateReplacementFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Fee for a new certificate when one is lost or has errors",Value:"Rs. 250 by demand draft in the name of the Director of General Education",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.1 A 16, p.6"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"Order printed with the manual",Value:[{Date:"2025-09-12",Title:"Sasthrolsavam to be held from school level this year",Text:"By order No. DGE/7858/2024 dated 12 September 2025 the Additional Director (Academic) of the Directorate of General Education issued the revised Sasthrolsavam Manual 2025 and gave the direction to hold the Sasthrolsavam from school level this year. The order refers to Government orders (Rt) No. 146/2025/GEDN dated 23 August 2025, No. 118/2024/GEDN dated 20 September 2024 and No. 116/2024/GEDN dated 19 September 2024.",Url:"https://mela.kite.kerala.gov.in/2026/entry_forms/sasthrolsavam_manual_2025.pdf"}],Source:"Manual 2025 order page, PDF p.1"},{Key:"AffiliationFeeUP",Kind:"fee",Label:"Affiliation fee of a UP school to the sub-district Work Experience Association or Council",Value:"Rs. 75 per UP school",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.9, Sub-district Work Experience Association, point 8, p.161"},{Key:"AffiliationFeeHS",Kind:"fee",Label:"Affiliation fee of a high school to the sub-district Work Experience Association or Council",Value:"Rs. 200 per high school",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.9, Sub-district Work Experience Association, point 8, p.161"},{Key:"AffiliationFeeHSS",Kind:"fee",Label:"Affiliation fee of an HSS or VHSS school to the sub-district Work Experience Association or Council",Value:"Rs. 300 per HSS or VHSS school",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.9, Sub-district Work Experience Association, point 8, p.161"},{Key:"StateAffiliationFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Affiliation fee a revenue district pays to the state Work Experience Association or Council",Value:"Rs. 400 per revenue district",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.9, State Work Experience Association, p.164"},{Key:"OnTheSpotStartTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Time the competition starts",Value:"9.30 a.m.",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.9, Revised time schedule, p.127"},{Key:"OnTheSpotEndTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Time the on-the-spot competition ends",Value:"12.30 p.m.",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.9, Revised time schedule, p.127"},{Key:"FinalEvaluationEndTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Time the final evaluation of the on-the-spot competition ends",Value:"1.30 p.m.",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.9, Revised time schedule, p.127"},{Key:"LunchEndTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Time lunch and the preparation for the exhibition competition end",Value:"2.30 p.m.",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.9, Revised time schedule, p.127"},{Key:"ExhibitionEndTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Time the exhibition competition and its evaluation end",Value:"4.30 p.m.",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.9, Revised time schedule, p.127"},{Key:"PublicViewingStartTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Time the public can start to view the products",Value:"3.30 p.m.",Source:"Manual 2025 Ch.9, Revised time schedule, p.127"}],l=[{Claim:"Rules for every fair (categories, levels, eligibility, online entry, grades, appeals, championship, committees, judges) and the Work Experience Fair chapter (levels, exhibition, time schedule, associations, the 25 and 35 on-the-spot items with their instructions) are taken from the manual. The entry forms and annexures at the end of the manual were read for the entry steps and the exhibition evaluation sheet.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Kerala School Sasthrolsavam Manual 2025, General Education Department, Government of Kerala, Chapters 1-5, Chapter 9 and the annexures",Url:"https://mela.kite.kerala.gov.in/2026/entry_forms/sasthrolsavam_manual_2025.pdf"},{Claim:"The list of items per group (LP, UP, HS, HSS/VHSS) and the item type (individual) is the official 2026 item list.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Kerala School Sasthrolsavam Item List 2026, KITE (Kerala Infrastructure and Technology for Education)",Url:"https://mela.kite.kerala.gov.in/2026/index.php/Home/item_list"}],d={TemplateKey:e,Year:2025,Note:t,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:o,AgeGroups:a,Competitions:i,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:r,Evidence:l};export{a as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,i as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,n as Page,o as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,h as Year,d as default};
